# Byte-compiled / cache
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Logs
*.log

# Intermediate pipeline data (regenerable from psx_data_8years/ via
# clean_data.py + feature_engineering.py, not needed to run the Streamlit
# app). psx_data_8years/ itself IS committed (small, ~2MB): the daily
# automation workflow (.github/workflows/daily_scrape.yml) appends to it
# incrementally on each run and needs the prior history to diff against and
# to persist across the workflow's ephemeral runners.
processed/
data/train.csv
data/test.csv
data/validate.csv
data/final_validation.csv

# master_dataset.csv: same category as the above - regenerable from
# psx_data_8years/ via merge_and_split.py (which the daily workflow already
# runs every time), and app.py only ever reads phase9_predictions.csv /
# phase9_top_drivers.csv, never this file directly. Moved here during the
# KSE-100 expansion (Phases/kse_100_expand.md) once it grew past GitHub's
# 100MB per-file push limit at 97 tickers - a 25-ticker version fit under
# the limit, but that was incidental, not a property to depend on.
data/master_dataset.csv

# Large model files, too big for a normal git push (several sit right at
# GitHub's 100MB per-file limit). phase7_rf_* predates Phase 9's Open/Close
# retrain and is kept here since app.py still serves off it until Phase 8 is
# redone (Phases/phase_9.md "Not in this phase"); phase9_rf_* is its
# Open/Close successor - the 10 combos generate_predictions.py needs are
# published as GitHub Release assets and downloaded by
# .github/workflows/daily_scrape.yml instead. phase10_rf_* isn't used by
# generate_predictions.py at all (it's hardcoded to phase9_ models), so it
# stays local-only.
models/phase7_rf_*.pkl
models/phase9_rf_*.pkl
models/phase10_rf_*.pkl

# Never-selected Phase 9 combos, kept for reference but not needed to run
# the app - see manage_model_storage.py / Phases/phase_9_notes.md. The 3
# Random Forest files here are handled like the ones above (GitHub Release
# asset, not git). The 3 GRU .pt files are tiny (~32KB) and generate_
# predictions.py needs them at inference time, so those are committed
# directly rather than adding a 4th storage path for 96KB total.
models_evaluation_only/*
!models_evaluation_only/phase9_gru_close_1d.pt
!models_evaluation_only/phase9_gru_close_20d.pt
!models_evaluation_only/phase9_gru_open_1d.pt

# TensorBoard training logs - local training artifact, not needed to run
# the app or the automation.
runs/

# Streamlit run artifacts
streamlit_run.log
streamlit_stdout.log
streamlit_stderr.log
